+<!-- ============ §3E Continual Learning ============ -->
+<h2 id="continual-learning">03E · Continual learning — from use traces to adapters</h2>
+<p class="lede">
+The "auto fine-tuning as you use the model" idea belongs here. Epistemos is not only a retrieval shell around MLX. The intended Pro/Research path is a closed learning loop: every run produces typed traces, the traces become training examples, training produces small adapters, adapters are routed back into inference, and promotion is gated by ACS, WBO drift, rollback, and visible falsifiers.
+</p>
+<p>
+The important distinction is that the base model remains a stable, auditable runtime. The system learns through <em class="k">attached deltas</em>: QLoRA / DoRA adapters, KTO preference updates, MoLoRA expert routes, and eventually L_SE fast-weight or Titans-style memory updates. That keeps learning local and personal without letting an unverified mutation silently become policy authority.
+</p>
