+<!-- ============ §3I Research Construction Engine ============ -->
+<h2 id="research-construction-engine">03I · AI research construction engine — the Erdős unlock</h2>
+<p class="lede">
+The OpenAI unit-distance result matters to Epistemos because it is a clean demonstration of the exact loop this app should make local: a model searched for a construction, imported machinery from a distant field, produced a proof candidate, and the result survived expert verification. The architectural lesson is not "ask a chatbot harder questions." It is: <em class="k">turn research itself into a typed, testable, local substrate workflow.</em>
+</p>
+<p>
+In the Erdős problem, the old intuition was geometric: square-grid-like constructions looked optimal. The new construction crossed into algebraic number theory and beat the obvious coordinate system. That is the performance moral for Epistemos: a unified cognitive substrate should not merely store everything in one place; it should search for the coordinate chart, kernel, route, memory tier, adapter, or proof representation that makes the same object cheaper, faster, and more verifiable.
+</p>
