+<h3>Performance synthesis</h3>
+<p>
+The practical win is not that the app becomes faster by chanting "lattice." The win is that one object can be re-expressed in whichever coordinate chart makes the next operation cheapest: a pixel tile when rendering, a vector when searching, an EML term when proving, a graph neighborhood when recalling, a KV page when decoding, a Metal buffer when executing. The unified substrate gives the system a common identity for all of those views, so optimization becomes route selection rather than lossy translation.
+</p>
+
+<table>
+  <thead><tr><th>Optimization</th><th>What changes</th><th>Why it matters</th><th>Floor test</th></tr></thead>
+  <tbody>
+    <tr><td>Copy-count collapse</td><td>Pixel, tensor, note span, graph node, and proof witness point to the same UAS object instead of separate duplicated payloads.</td><td>Less memory pressure, fewer Swift↔Rust↔Metal↔MLX transfers, cleaner provenance.</td><td><span class="tag todo">F-UAS-CopyCount</span></td></tr>
+    <tr><td>Active support minimization</td><td>Active Assembly wakes the smallest sufficient support set instead of passing the whole vault or whole graph to the model.</td><td>Lower prompt cost, faster local inference, better citation discipline.</td><td><span class="tag todo">F-ActiveAssembly-Minimal</span></td></tr>
+    <tr><td>Kernel fusion</td><td>Repeated EML / Scan / Geometry patterns become one specialized Metal or Rust kernel when the proof and CPU reference agree.</td><td>Hot loops stop paying interpreter and allocation overhead.</td><td><span class="tag gated">F-ULP + kernel parity</span></td></tr>
+    <tr><td>RouteProfile optimization</td><td>The route chooser compares deterministic, embedding, small-model, mid-model, cloud, and proof routes as projections of one request.</td><td>The app can pick the cheapest route that still satisfies witness and capability gates.</td><td><span class="tag todo">routeProfiles() production table</span></td></tr>
+    <tr><td>Adapter locality</td><td>Learning becomes small local deltas attached to object families, not blind mutation of the base model.</td><td>Supports "auto fine-tune as you use it" without corrupting the global model.</td><td><span class="tag gated">WBO drift + rollback ledger</span></td></tr>
