+<!-- ============ §16 Math ============ -->
+<h2 id="math">16 · The math, briefly</h2>
+<div class="split">
+  <div class="split-tag math">E4 / H1</div>
+  <div class="split-body"><strong>WBO-7 Master Inequality.</strong> The end-to-end output of a pipeline of approximating stages is bounded by the sum of per-stage Wyner-Ziv budgets.
+    <div class="math">‖ŷ − y‖ ≤ Σᵢ βᵢ      where βᵢ = WBO budget of stage i</div>
+    <strong>Status:</strong> Proven in Lean (E4) and operationally enforced in code (H1). Every <code>LatticeBudget</code> on a <code>cognitive_dag</code> node pays into this ledger.
+  </div>
 </div>
+
+<div class="split">
+  <div class="split-tag math">H4</div>
+  <div class="split-body"><strong>LatticeCoder / Babai quantization.</strong> For a lattice Λ ⊂ ℝⁿ and target vector t, Babai's nearest-plane algorithm gives x ∈ Λ with
+    <div class="math">‖t − x‖ ≤ (1/2)·√(Σᵢ ‖bᵢ*‖²)   (Gram-Schmidt bound)</div>
+    <strong>Status:</strong> Proven (classical Babai). Used to bound the quantization stage of E4's pipeline.
   </div>
-</section>
+</div>
 
